      "unit": "cabin_boy",
      "cell": [
        14,
        3
      ],
      "facing": [
        0,
        1
      ],
      "wander": 3,
      "chatter": [
        "Every net on the frames and not one of them wet since spring.",
        "Halbrec says the tide brings things back. He never says what."
      ],
      "talk": {
        "hello": [
          "Every net on the frames and not one of them wet since spring. What can I get you?",
          "Ahoy. That's a joke. We say ahoy here as a joke."
        ],
        "ask": [
          {
            "q": "Who keeps the light?",
            "a": "Nobody, since the keeper went up one night and didn't come down. It still turns. Don't ask me how. I asked once and didn't sleep for a week."
          },
          {
            "q": "Why don't the boats go out?",
            "a": "Gates by sea. You can't see them till you're through one."
          }
        ],
        "news": true,
        "sells": [
          {
            "item": "bread"
          },
          {
            "item": "ale_flask"
          },
          {
            "item": "salt_pouch",
            "price": 55
          }
        ],
        "shop": "Salt, ale, and bread that's only a bit salty.",
        "bye": "Fair winds. Or any winds. We'd take any winds."
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "a gull with a temper",
      "unit": "flame_dove",
      "cell": [
        17,
        11
      ],
      "facing": [
        -1,
        0
      ],
      "wander": 5,
      "chatter": [
        "It has taken two hats and a knife off this beach today."
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Nettle the Cutpurse",
      "unit": "hat_fox",
      "cell": [
        8,
        9
      ],
      "facing": [
        1,
        0
      ],
      "wander": 4,
      "chatter": [
        "There is no law down here, only tide tables.",
        "Count your coin before the shingle and after it."
      ],
      "talk": {
        "refuse": {
          "text": "Nettle looks straight through you, at the tide.",
          "chance": 1.0,
          "unless": "nettle:won",
          "check": {
            "skill": "wits",
            "dc": 12
          },
          "check_q": "Mention the tide tables are wrong.",
          "won": "...They're not wrong. They're forged. Who told you? Sit down.",
          "won_flag": "nettle:won",
          "still_no": "Nettle smiles at the sea. Not at you.",
          "leave": "Leave her to the tide."
        },
        "hello": "There's no law down here, only tide tables. Which you've noticed are wrong.",
        "ask": [
          {
            "q": "Who forged them?",
            "a": "Somebody who wants the boats in at the wrong hour. Ask the pirate. Ask him while he's sober, if you can find the hour."
          }
        ],
        "bye": "Low tide's at dusk. Really."
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "the Tidewalker",
      "unit": "sea_man",
      "cell": [
        16,
        9
      ],
      "facing": [
        1,
        0
      ],
      "story_npc": "sea_man",
      "talk": {
        "hello": [
          "Tide's turning. You can hear it if you stop talking.",
          "Mind the nets. They've been kind to me."
        ],
        "again": [
          "You came back on the tide. Most things do.",
          "The water's darker than when you left."
        ],
        "ask": [
          {
            "q": "Where are you from?",
            "a": "Out there. A ship broke on the shoals in the storm that drowned three ports. They tell me I was on it. I remember the cold, and the lion."
          },
          {
            "q": "What's wrong with the water?",
            "a": "It's turning black at the edges. Something is seeping up from far down. The reef things are coming in angry."
          },
          {
            "q": "Is that lion made of water?",
            "a": "Mostly. It doesn't explain itself. Neither do I."
          }
        ],
        "bye": [
          "Fair winds.",
          "Keep your feet dry while you can."
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "the Tide Lion",
      "unit": "tide_lion",
      "cell": [
        17,
        10
      ],
